DISABLED — 2026-09-04, Sprint 1.1 document cleanup.

Renamed to `.md.disabled` so it no longer appears as a runnable workflow,
matching how generate-project-sync.yml and update-master-date.yml were handled.

Why:
  1. It auto-pushes to `main`. Steps 6-11 run `git add .`, commit with a fixed
     generic message ("chore: refactor and update code"), and `git push origin
     main` — several marked `// turbo`, so they run without confirmation. The
     project's working agreement is a sprint branch, a reviewed diff, then a
     merge and a tag. This bypasses all of it.
  2. Its build steps are already broken. `npm run lint` and `npm run build`
     refer to the Vite/React/ESLint setup that Sprint 1.1 Task 3 replaces with
     Astro. `npm run lint` has no equivalent in the scaffold's package.json.
  3. A generic commit message on an unreviewed `git add .` is how unrelated
     project metadata arrived in this repo in the first place.

When to revisit: after Sprint 1.1 Task 3, if a per-project agent workflow is
still wanted. It would need a real lint/build target for Astro, and it should
stop at the commit — pushing to `main` stays a human decision.

Original contents preserved verbatim below.
