1. Run linting to check for code issues
// turbo
2. npm run lint
3. Analyze the linting output. If there are errors, fix them. If there are warnings or improvement opportunities, refactor the code.
4. Verify that the application builds successfully
// turbo
5. npm run build
6. Stage all changes
// turbo
7. git add .
8. Commit the changes with a descriptive message summarizing the updates
9. git commit -m "chore: refactor and update code"
10. Push changes to remote origin main
// turbo
11. git push origin main
